## pnpm's supply-chain trust check flags eslint-import-resolver-typescript@3.10.1
## and semver@6.3.1 (transitive deps of eslint-config-next, lint-tooling only --
## never shipped to users) as "trust downgrades": their currently-locked
## versions lack npm provenance attestation that an earlier published version
## had. This is a false-positive pattern affecting much of the ecosystem right
## after pnpm introduced the check, not a specific finding about either
## package -- ignoring downgrades on packages published more than 30 days ago
## avoids blocking every `pnpm install`/`pnpm dev` on it without disabling the
## check entirely for genuinely new/recent packages.
trustPolicyIgnoreAfter=43200
